     wwllaann__xxaauutthh — External authenticator support for 802.11 devices

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddeevviiccee wwllaann__xxaauutthh

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwllaann__xxaauutthh module is a wlan(4) authenticator plugin for use with
     user-mode authentication implementations such as hhoossttaappdd.  It hooks into
     the 802.11 layer and does nothing.  As a result, 802.11 stations that as‐
     sociate are not authorized to send or receive frames until they are au‐
     thorized by an external agent; typically using a protocol such as WPA,
     802.1x, or 802.11i.

     This module is automatically loaded by the rc script that normally starts
     hostapd(8).

